L224: Subsequently, the protein expression of TET2 in fetal skeletal muscle at embryonic day 18.5 (e18.5) was examined. In alignment with the results observed in myogenic cells, significantly elevated protein levels of TET2 and SVCT2 were detected in fetal skeletal muscle of the M‐Ex group compared to the M‐Con group (Figure  6e–g ). Moreover, the catalytic activity of TET dioxygenases for 5mC oxidation requires Fe 2+  and α‐KG as cofactors. [ 
